# Ad Segment Detection in Video

AI Engineer take-home project for detecting advertisement segments inside videos.

The system accepts a video URL, processes audio and visual evidence, and returns advertisement segments in machine-readable JSON.

The pipeline is designed for:

* long-form YouTube videos
* YouTube Shorts
* Instagram Reels through local/direct media input
* live-stream processing as a design extension

---

# 1. Current Status

The main pipeline components are implemented:

* YouTube acquisition using `yt-dlp`
* audio extraction using FFmpeg
* timestamped transcription using `faster-whisper`
* rule-based and LLM-based audio ad detection
* frame sampling
* OpenCV candidate-frame filtering
* local vision-language-model classification
* audio/visual fusion
* FastAPI HTTP endpoint
* manual `ground_truth.json`
* `DESIGN.md`
* `EVAL.md`

The main current limitation is local VLM inference speed.

`qwen3-vl:4b` is running locally through Ollama on CPU. Individual image classifications can take several minutes on my machine.

Because of this, I tested the visual model on real selected candidate frames but did not complete a full end-to-end visual pass over every candidate for all five supplied videos.

A faster CPU or GPU-backed Ollama environment should reduce this inference bottleneck, but the current submission should be treated as partially validated rather than a fully benchmarked production pipeline.

---

